{
  "id": 408843610,
  "iid": 20978,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Clean up sync pipe read code.",
  "description": "Ensure that pipe_read_bytes() is never asked to read a number of bytes\nthat won't fit in an ssize_t, so that it will return either -1 on an\nerror or a positive number on success. (That should, in practice, always\nbe the case, as it'll either be reading a 4-byte message header or an\namount of data that is 2^24-1 bytes or less.)\n\nFirst check for a return value of -1 before checking whether the return\nvalue is equal to the number of bytes requested; that ensures that, when\ndoing said comparison, we can cast the number of bytes returned to\nsize_t and avoid a signed vs. unsigned comparison warning. (That's not\nnecessary when reading the 4-byte header, as the constant 4 is an int.)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2025-08-21T09:50:44.217Z",
