      "id": "109468f1215314b00e622eb3e7125d30fdbfffb2",
      "short_id": "109468f1",
      "created_at": "2025-08-21T21:05:06.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "9fe7d2576f7cb2335661bdf9dddccfba4677344e"
      ],
      "title": "Clean up sync pipe read code.",
      "message": "Clean up sync pipe read code.\n\nEnsure that pipe_read_bytes() is never asked to read a number of bytes\nthat won't fit in an ssize_t, so that it will return either -1 on an\nerror or a positive number on success. (That should, in practice, always\nbe the case, as it'll either be reading a 4-byte message header or an\namount of data that is 2^24-1 bytes or less.)\n\nFirst check for a return value of -1 before checking whether the return\nvalue is equal to the number of bytes requested; that ensures that, when\ndoing said comparison, we can cast the number of bytes returned to\nsize_t and avoid a signed vs. unsigned comparison warning. (That's not\nnecessary when reading the 4-byte header, as the constant 4 is an int.)\n",
      "author_name": "Guy Harris",
      "author_email": "gharris@sonic.net",
      "authored_date": "2025-08-21T02:50:04.000-07:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-08-21T21:05:06.000+00:00",
